The supporting results measure different things:
- sub-steps inside one circuit (previous-token, then induction);
- staggering across heads: 2410.02984 (1:7 before 1:6) and 2606.02378 (final heads joining at 80B or 3048B tokens);
- stages in the ICL strategy, uniform→unigram→bigram (2402.11004): strategy alignment confirms an abrupt unigram-to-bigram switch after a prolonged intermediate stage, without separately identifying every head-formation step;
- refinements after the first formation: lw:tiEgivi7crHSnSrH5 (second transition at 530M–620M tokens).
The statement does not say which of these counts as formation.
